     "ORGANISE MAY USE ITS OWN ADDITIONS AS FAST-FORWARD ENDPOINTS, so the law is partly self-justifying: organise adds a node, authors an edge through it, and O3 confirms the edge because the node organise added is in `nodes`. Constructed and machine-checked at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:101 -- on the recorded inputs a node-set-conformant implementation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:72) returns the edge 26-25, and BOTH its endpoints are nodes organise itself added (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:90). The cost is not visible on any recorded run: see :measurement-that-separates-them.",
     :run-by
