     :costs
     "THE READING IS ONE PROPOSITION WITH TWO CONTENTS, and which it has is decided by D1 rather than by this choice. At CascadeDiff the field is `selected ∪ admittedBy`, which is the whole recorded node set (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:46), and the recorded edge 18-19 is inside it (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:200). At the function carrier `Cascade` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-35) has no `admittedBy` field, so the same reading is just the caller's selection and NO conformant function returns the recorded edge on the recorded selected input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:172) -- the selected arm's cost, inherited. Stated against overstating it: on the recorded selected input the no-bootstrap relation is EMPTY (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:128), so the separation above is checked against a relation shown inhabited on a constructed input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:162) and not on a recorded one.",
