  :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding
  {:all-arms-run
   "2026-09-07, F12 slice 18. All three arms C541 section 4's D3 names -- the two after-the-law routes and the refusal -- carry measured :buys and :costs, each run by slice 15 (futon2 652f4805) with its plant read back before the worker that measured it. Arm B additionally carries slice 16's measurements at the three non-primary denominators (futon2 23f22dc5). One gap is named rather than hidden and is recorded under :what-would-change-the-measurement: arm A was measured at the primary denominator only. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is still :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key.",
   :not-claimed
   "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED: :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. This entry does not say that an after-the-law encoding is admissible or that it is not; it says what each of the three answers is measured to cost. It does NOT restate the un-fitting guard: C541 section 4 says that restatement is owed IF the answer is yes, and no answer is taken here, so the guard stands as written at futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57. It takes no position on the gate's :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then failure, which belongs to whoever owns that table. It says nothing about D1 (which carrier the four O-laws are stated of, registered as :organise-carrier), about D2 (which denominator O4 is read over, registered as :organise-o4-denominator), about the third origin (:organise-third-origin), about the O3 field question (:organise-o3-field), or about the sorry (:organise-sorry), which at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is still neither discharged nor amended. Registering this choice ran no machine and wrote no source file: the arms were run by slice 15, which made every plant in a temporary copy and left futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj and every file under futon3:checks/ unmodified.",
   :what-would-change-the-measurement
   "A RECORDED RUN IN WHICH TWO RULE-BEARING PATTERNS BOTH ACT, PRODUCED BY THE GATE RATHER THAN BY A PLANT -- which would settle D3 by making it moot rather than by answering it, since every number above other than arm C's comes from a temporary copy. That needs the THEN-correspondence failure repaired by whoever owns the rule table, 3 of 4 at HEAD (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:264-272). Short of that, two measurements would move this entry: arm A run at the paired, transcript and full-play denominators, which no artifact carries (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:109 reads the primary arm alone), and a construction on which the two member-carried rules contend INSIDE the primary cohort, which neither arm supplies -- arm A gives zero primary contentions (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12) and arm B gives three, all outside it (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:30).",
   :evidence
   "holes/labs/wm-contract/C553-F12-d3-encoding.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj; holes/labs/wm-contract/C541-F12-o4-reachability.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C554-F12-d2-denominator.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn",
   :question
   "O4 says that where the precedence changed, the acting order or the score changed with it (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538). Exercising it needs a cascade two of whose members carry rules, and no recorded run has one: the maximum rule-carrying member count over the nine records is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265). Reaching two therefore means changing the apparatus after the law is already written -- either a construction over a tension chosen so the find selects two rule-bearing patterns, or a new play-grain encoding of a THEN a member already carries -- or refusing both and leaving O4 unexercised. The zaif rule table's whole standing is that it was committed before the run and not fitted to it, and its STATED un-fitting guard covers fitting to a WIN: `a table written to make the cascade win would not carry rules for patterns the cascade does not contain` (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57), computed by membership (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:479-480) and failing only when that collection is empty (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585). It says nothing about fitting to a LAW, which is the intervention this question is about. This is D3, raised at C541 section 4 with two routes and the refusal. This entry registers all three with what each is measured to cost.",
   :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge],
   :status :observed-not-decided,
   :at "2026-09-07",
   :measurement-that-separates-them
   "THE ARMS SEPARATE ON WHETHER O4 BECOMES EXERCISABLE, NOT ON WHETHER IT BECOMES TRUE -- no arm produces a true O4 at the denominator the gate grades. Arm A moves the carrying count 1 -> 2 and leaves the primary verdict false with zero contending primary rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:2, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:5, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12); arm B moves the status :not-exercised -> :exercised-false (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:136, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:15); arm C leaves zero (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:246). THE ONE PLANT THAT DOES MOVE THE PRIMARY VERDICT TO TRUE IS A NEGATIVE CONTROL, NOT AN ARM: broadening an existing member-carried rule so it is live on primary rounds gives :primary-o4-true (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:256-259, planted at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:160-165), and it is in the control set precisely because it is the edit that would make the law pass. So on everything measured, D3 and D2 are not independent: an affirmative D3 buys a TRUE O4 only if D2 also reads the law off a denominator wider than primary, where arm B gives true three times over (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1396, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1562, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:802). Three further controls fix what each measurement is sensitive to, each plant read back before its worker ran (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:35-40, hard-failing at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:210-216): renaming the fifth rule to a nonmember returns O4 to :not-exercised (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:248-251), killing its antecedent takes it from 102 live rounds to none (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:252-255), and fitting every rule id to a member fires the un-fitting guard (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:260-263).",
   :row :F12,
   :arms
   [{:arm :construct-a-cascade-that-selects-two-rule-bearing-patterns,
     :run-by "F12 slice 15 (C553); futon2 652f4805",
     :what-it-is
     "C541 section 4's first route -- change WHAT THE FIND SELECTS. Measured by planting the second rule-bearing pattern, war-machine/ambient-pattern-retrieval, into the marginal-gain-floor arm of a TEMPORARY COPY of the cascade record and bumping that run's member count, then re-running slice 3's reachability report against the copy (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:89-104, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:106-121). The plant is read back and cross-checked against the member count before the arm is measured (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:102-104).",
     :buys
     "THE PRECONDITION, AND ONLY THAT. The maximum rule-carrying member count moves 1 -> 2 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:2 against the premise at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265), so slice 3's :not-a-witness blocker -- no constructor selected both patterns, so there is no cascade for an O4 row to be OF -- is the one thing this arm removes.",
     :costs
     "IT BUYS NO WITNESS. Over the same 29 primary rounds the primary O4 is still FALSE: the acting order does not change and the score stands at 14 -> 14, with zero contending primary rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:4-8, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12). Nothing else moves either -- the cohort still carries 103 rounds and the primary denominator still 29 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:10-11). So answering D3 in the affirmative on this route leaves O4 exactly where it was unless D2 moves off the primary denominator too, which is a second choice (:organise-o4-denominator) and not this one. UNMEASURED AND NOT GUESSED: this arm was run at the primary denominator alone (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:109), so what it would give at paired, transcript or full play is not recorded anywhere -- unlike the arm below, which slice 16 did carry to the other three."}
