     :run-by
     "F12 slice 15 (C553); futon2 652f4805. Slice 16 (C554; futon2 23f22dc5) then measured THE SAME ENCODING at the other three denominators, using this arm's rule value rather than copying it (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:190-192, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:24-31).",
     :what-it-is
     "C541 section 4's second route -- change WHAT A SELECTED MEMBER CAN DO. A fifth rule is added to the play-grain rule table encoding the authored THEN of aif/status-gated-belief-update, a pattern the cascade ALREADY carries, citing the span futon3:library/aif/status-gated-belief-update.flexiarg:26-30; the plant goes into a temporary copy of the gate placed first on the worker's classpath and is read back before the worker runs (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:24-33, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:35-40, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:42-53, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:146-148).",
     :buys
     "IT IS THE ONLY ARM THAT MAKES O4 EXERCISABLE AT ALL. The primary O4 status moves :not-exercised -> :exercised-false (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:136, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:15, exercised? true at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:238); the fifth rule is live on 102 rounds including all 29 primary ones (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:32-134, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:137-166); and the two member-carried rules contend on rounds 3, 4 and 7 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:16-28), the first contention between two rules the cascade actually carries -- slice 3's contention at the same rounds dropped the membership filter deliberately, because only one member carried a rule and the gate's own contention over members is empty (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn:335-337, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn:186). AT EVERY DENOMINATOR OTHER THAN PRIMARY THE SAME ENCODING GIVES O4 TRUE: paired, contention at round 7, score 15 -> 15, true by the acting-order disjunct alone (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1389, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1394-1398); transcript, contention at 3, 4 and 7 with the score moving 20 -> 19 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1555, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1560-1564, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1878-1879); full play, the same contention with the score at 21 -> 20 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:794-804, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1119-1120). Every non-primary TRUE that :organise-o4-denominator records as its Arm B rests on THIS arm being admitted.",
     :costs
     "THE VERDICT IT MAKES POSSIBLE IS FALSE WHERE THE GATE GRADES. At the primary denominator the precedence exchange [8 3] -> [3 8] changes neither the acting order -- the before and after vectors are identical, each 29 entries of the fifth rule alone, the other member-carried rule firing on no primary round (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:178-207, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:208-237, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:239-240) -- nor the score, 15 -> 15 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:241-242), so O4 does not hold (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:31) and all three contentions fall outside the cohort (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:30). AND THE STATED UN-FITTING GUARD DOES NOT FIRE ON IT, which is a cost and not a clearance: three rules remain outside the cascade after the plant (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:167-170, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:176) and the guard fails only on an empty collection (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585), so the one intervention D3 is about passes a guard written about a different one. That the guard CAN fire is checked rather than assumed -- fitting every rule id to a cascade member empties the collection and fires it (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:260-263). This is why an affirmative answer on this route owes the restatement C541 section 4 names, and the restatement is not written here."}
    {:arm :refuse-both-after-the-law-interventions,
