  :organise-o4-denominator
  {:all-arms-run
   "2026-09-07, F12 slice 20, registering the run slice 19 made (futon2 3c0ad833). ALL FIVE ARMS NOW CARRY MEASURED :buys AND :costs. Slice 17 registered four and named the fifth as unrun together with what running it would take -- one more denominator spec reading the two fields from two round sets (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:20-23, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:44-71) -- and slice 19 built exactly that (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:88-138) and ran it on both constructions, the acceptance run printing :problems [] (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6157). THIS KEY REPLACES :arms-not-all-run, WHICH SLICE 19'S OWN RUN MADE FALSE and which C555 named as the stale claim rather than leaving it to be found. The fifth arm's verdicts are pinned like the other arms' so a later run reports a move instead of silently restating today's numbers (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:376-379), and three plants each move the acceptance run off PASS: reading the score over the acting-order round set (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:380-387), giving the identity collapse a paired order side (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:388-392), and making the forced-empty side non-empty (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:98-101, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:393-395). STILL NO ARM IS PREFERRED and no verdict is taken on O4 itself; :status remains :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key.",
   :not-claimed
   "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED: :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. This entry does not say O4 holds or that it fails -- every verdict above is a verdict AT a denominator, and the entry's content is that they differ. It says nothing about D1 (which carrier the four O-laws are stated of, registered as :organise-carrier), about D3 (whether an O4 witness may be reached by an encoding written after the law, registered as :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding), about the third origin (:organise-third-origin), about the O3 field question (:organise-o3-field), or about the sorry (:organise-sorry), which at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is still neither discharged nor amended. It takes no position on the gate's :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then failure, which belongs to whoever owns that table. Registering this choice ran no machine and wrote no source file: the first four arms were run by slice 16 and the fifth by slice 19, and this entry only records them. NOR IS THE FIFTH ARM PREFERRED BY BEING LAST: five measured arms are five verdicts AT a reading.",
   :what-would-change-the-measurement
   "A RECORDED RUN IN WHICH TWO RULE-BEARING PATTERNS BOTH ACT -- which would move every arm's numbers off a plant and onto the corpus. The maximum rule-carrying member count on any recorded run is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn), and the gate that would produce such a run does not pass at HEAD: require-pass! aborts with :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then for three of four rules, with :file-exists? and :pattern-id-matches-path? true for all four and :span-inside-the-then-block? false for three (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:579-582, thrown at futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:589-591, recomputed into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6105-6156), and that rule table is not :F12's to repair. Until then, whether a plant may supply the second rule at all is D3's question, measured by slice 15 into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn and registered by slice 18 as :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding, whose Arm B is where every non-primary TRUE recorded above comes from.",
   :evidence
   "holes/labs/wm-contract/C554-F12-d2-denominator.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C555-F12-d2-fifth-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj; holes/labs/wm-contract/C541-F12-o4-reachability.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C553-F12-d3-encoding.md",
   :question
   "O4 is a three-way disjunction -- the precedence did not change, OR the acting order changed, OR the score changed (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538) -- and it does not say WHICH ROUNDS the acting order and the score are read over. The gate's agreement number is computed over the primary cohort because a comparison needs a determined oracle label, but O4 makes no reference to an oracle: an acting order is something the cascade does whether or not the record can grade it. The denominator is therefore free, and it is not a free hand that leaves the verdict alone -- on the recorded run one and the same precedence exchange over one and the same rule pair gives O4 FALSE over the 29 primary rounds and TRUE over the 49 paired and the 102 transcript rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4903-4907, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4976-4980, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5089-5093). This is D2, raised at C541 section 4 with three options. This entry registers those options with what each is measured to cost, and adds the fourth the checker ran.",
   :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge],
   :status :observed-not-decided,
